{"title":"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A truncated cone has horizontal bases with radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. A sphere is tangent to the top, bottom, and lateral surface of the truncated cone. What is the radius of the sphere? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a394e5e5873a57c973dc4eac1dc7523a33e730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 4\\sqrt{5} \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 9 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 10 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 6\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"402\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trapezoid\" title=\"Trapezoid\">trapezoid</a> (label it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> as follows) cross-section of the truncate cone along a diameter of the bases:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b290d343dc7c6049f7d45f5f1abc749c2af3d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(220); defaultpen(0.7); pair A = (0,0), B = (36,0), C = (20,12), D = (16,12), E=(A+B)/2, F=(20+1.6,12-1.2), G = (C+D)/2; draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(circumcircle(E,F,G)); dot(E); dot(F); dot(G); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,F,NE); label(&quot;\\(G\\)&quot;,G,N); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"162\" /></center>\n<p>Above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/7/15702fb3f7b1aeaefff24913baf2a387bdd2d54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,F,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are points of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent_(geometry)\" title=\"Tangent (geometry)\">tangency</a>. By the Two Tangent Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac620755efb30ffff0ad4de5c51d4c6f7516a0ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF = BE = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca669f780faf25a2a5171adba0031242c5509f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = CG = 2$\" width=\"114\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3df80c6052a2128b30eb8a39a49d8ed45409800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. We draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> such that it is the foot of the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be32165967b3173aa255274dec44b971d06e9cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{HD}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />: \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df55cbef93e6c3485f8c0d77176293f0fe2bcb3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(220); defaultpen(0.7); pair A = (0,0), B = (36,0), C = (20,12), D = (16,12), E=(A+B)/2, F=(20+1.6,12-1.2), G = (C+D)/2, H=(16,0); pair P=(D+G)/2, Q=(D+H)/2, R=(B+E)/2, T=(A+H)/2, O=(E+G)/2; draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(G--E--H--D); draw(circumcircle(E,F,G)); dot(E);dot(F);dot(G);dot(H);dot(O); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,S); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,F,NE); label(&quot;\\(G\\)&quot;,G,N); label(&quot;\\(H\\)&quot;,H,S); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,O,NE); label(&quot;\\(2\\)&quot;,P,N); label(&quot;\\(12\\)&quot;,Q,W); label(&quot;\\(18\\)&quot;,R,S); label(&quot;\\(16\\)&quot;,T,S); label(&quot;\\(20\\)&quot;,(A+D)/2,NW); label(&quot;\\(r\\)&quot;,(O+E)/2,SE); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"162\" /></center>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/33818f7f2c5ac679b0137c426359e70d0f71359e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{DH}2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{20^2 - 16^2}}2 = 12\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"40\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc5f8a0b3d0c3bc7e9000380526c2881dff9062b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{{A (6)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"55\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B\">2004 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problem